---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Camille Roux — Evolutionary Biology">
  <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-6xl flex-col">
    <SiteHeader current="home" />

    <!-- Presentation -->
        <section
          id="presentation"
          class="border-b border-[var(--line)] py-10 lg:py-14"
        >
          <h2 class="section-title">Presentation</h2>

          <div class="presentation-block presentation-narrative">
            <p>
              My scientific path started in Lille, where I completed my PhD with Xavier Vekemans
              and Vincent Castric between 2007 and 2010, in the laboratory of Genetics and
              Evolution of Plant Populations. The work focused on speciation in <em>Arabidopsis</em>,
              especially between <em>A. halleri</em> and <em>A. lyrata</em>, and on the evolution of
              heavy-metal accumulation. We showed that divergence between these species coincided
              with a major tandem triplication involved in the ability of <em>A. halleri</em> to
              hyperaccumulate zinc.
            </p>
            <p>
              A second line of the PhD examined the genomic consequences of balancing selection
              around the self-incompatibility locus, one of the strongest known examples of
              long-term balancing selection. Despite this intense selection, its genomic footprint
              remained highly localized.
            </p>
            <p>
              I then joined the Institut des Sciences de l'Évolution de Montpellier for a postdoc
              with Nicolas Bierne and Nicolas Galtier (2011–2013), based at the marine station in
              Sète. There, the main focus was a striking case of introgression between two
              <em>Ciona</em> species that remain able to produce viable and fertile hybrids despite
              being roughly fourteen times more divergent than humans and chimpanzees.
            </p>
            <p>
              From 2013 to 2016, I worked in Lausanne with John Pannell, first on methodological
              approaches for high-throughput sequencing data in polyploids, then on how plant
              metapopulation dynamics shape the evolution of reproductive systems. Since 2017, I
              have been a CNRS researcher, in Lille until 2025 and now at ISEM in Montpellier.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="presentation-block places-strip" aria-label="Places along this path">
            <figure class="place-card">
              <div class="place-card__image">
                <img
                  src="/images/cities/lille.png"
                  alt="Lille"
                  width="320"
                  height="240"
                  loading="lazy"
                  decoding="async"
                />
              </div>
              <figcaption>Lille</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="place-card">
              <div class="place-card__image">
                <img
                  src="/images/cities/sete.jpg"
                  alt="Sète"
                  width="320"
                  height="240"
                  loading="lazy"
                  decoding="async"
                />
              </div>
              <figcaption>Sète</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="place-card">
              <div class="place-card__image">
                <img
                  src="/images/cities/lausanne.jpeg"
                  alt="Lausanne"
                  width="320"
                  height="240"
                  loading="lazy"
                  decoding="async"
                />
              </div>
              <figcaption>Lausanne</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>

          <p class="presentation-block presentation-focus">
            My work seeks to understand the dynamics of the speciation process: when the first
            barriers to gene flow arise, and when genomes eventually become fully impermeable to
            gene flow. To address these questions, I combine population genomics, demographic
            inference, and comparative analyses.
          </p>

          <p class="presentation-block text-sm text-[var(--muted)] max-w-3xl">
            This work currently develops along three connected axes.
          </p>

          <div class="presentation-block grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3 lg:gap-5">
            <article
              class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--line)] bg-[var(--card)]/80 p-5 md:col-span-1"
            >
              <h3 class="text-base font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--green)]">
                Speciation genomics
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[var(--muted)]">
                Estimating genetic connectivity and reproductive isolation from genomic data,
                especially along the grey zone between populations and species.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article
              class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--line)] bg-[var(--card)]/80 p-5 md:col-span-1"
            >
              <h3 class="text-base font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--green)]">
                Methods and inference
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[var(--muted)]">
                Developing and applying ABC-based tools such as DILS to compare models of
                divergence, estimate gene flow, and account for linked selection.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article
              class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--line)] bg-[var(--card)]/80 p-5 md:col-span-1"
            >
              <h3 class="text-base font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--green)]">
                Comparative approaches
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[var(--muted)]">
                Comparing species pairs and clades to ask whether reproductive isolation
                accumulates at different rates across biological systems.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>

          <div class="presentation-block">
            <h3 class="presentation-subtitle">Current questions</h3>
            <p class="section-intro mt-3 max-w-3xl">
              A recent comparative analysis across hundreds of species pairs (<a
                href="https://www.science.org/doi/abs/10.1126/science.adl2356"
                class="text-[var(--green)] underline decoration-[var(--line)] underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:decoration-[var(--green)]"
                >Science, 2025</a
              >) found that plant lineages tend to be less genetically connected than animal
              lineages at comparable molecular divergence. That result is one anchor for ongoing
              work, and a starting point for asking which biological features accelerate or slow
              barrier accumulation.
            </p>

            <ul class="mt-6 flex max-w-3xl flex-col gap-3" role="list">
              <li class="question-line">
                Why do lineages differ in the rate at which barriers to gene flow accumulate?
              </li>
              <li class="question-line">
                How does genetic connectivity decline with molecular divergence?
              </li>
              <li class="question-line">
                Which genomic compartments and biological features contribute to reproductive
                isolation?
              </li>
              <li class="question-line">
                Can population-scale estimates of reproductive isolation be compared across
                clades?
              </li>
              <li class="question-line">
                Do evolutionary radiations coincide with faster declines in gene flow between
                closely related species?
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Selected work -->
        <section id="work" class="scroll-mt-8 border-b border-[var(--line)] py-12 lg:py-16">
          <h2 class="section-title">Selected work</h2>

          <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col divide-y divide-[var(--line)]">
            <article class="py-6 first:pt-0 lg:py-7">
              <p class="work-meta">Science · 2025</p>
              <h3 class="work-title">
                <a
                  href="https://doi.org/10.1126/science.adl2356"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                  >Rapid establishment of species barriers in plants compared with that in
                  animals</a
                >
              </h3>
              <p class="work-description">
                A comparative population genomic analysis showing that, for a given level of
                molecular divergence, plant species pairs are less genetically connected than
                animal species pairs.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article class="py-6 lg:py-7">
              <p class="work-meta">PLOS Biology · 2016</p>
              <h3 class="work-title">
                <a
                  href="https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.2000234"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                  >Shedding Light on the Grey Zone of Speciation along a Continuum of Genomic
                  Divergence</a
                >
              </h3>
              <p class="work-description">
                A conceptual and empirical contribution to thinking about speciation as a
                continuum rather than a binary transition.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article class="py-6 lg:py-7">
              <p class="work-meta">Molecular Ecology Resources · 2021</p>
              <h3 class="work-title">
                <a
                  href="https://doi.org/10.1111/1755-0998.13323"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                  >DILS: Demographic inferences with linked selection by using ABC</a
                >
              </h3>
              <p class="work-description">
                A method and software framework to compare demographic models, estimate gene
                flow, and account for linked selection in population genomic data.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article class="py-6 lg:py-7">
              <p class="work-meta">Peer Community Journal · 2024</p>
              <h3 class="work-title">
                <a
                  href="https://doi.org/10.24072/pcjournal.476"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                  >The impact of social complexity on the efficacy of natural selection in
                  termites</a
                >
              </h3>
              <p class="work-description">
                A comparative molecular evolution study asking how social organization affects
                the efficacy of natural selection.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article class="pb-0 pt-6 lg:py-7">
              <p class="work-meta">Methods in Molecular Biology · 2023</p>
              <h3 class="work-title">
                <a
                  href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-0716-2561-3_17"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                  >Inferring the Demographic History and Inheritance Mode of Tetraploid Species
                  Using ABC</a
                >
              </h3>
              <p class="work-description">
                An ABC framework to infer the demographic history, origin, and inheritance mode
                of tetraploid species from population genomic data.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Tools and approaches -->
        <section class="border-b border-[var(--line)] py-12 lg:py-16">
          <h2 class="section-title">Tools and approaches</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base leading-7 text-[var(--muted)]">
            Method development is part of how I work: ABC-based frameworks turn comparative
            questions about gene flow and reproductive isolation into quantities that can be
            estimated and compared across datasets. Code and tools are available on{" "}
            <a
              href="https://github.com/popgenomics/"
              class="text-[var(--green)] underline decoration-[var(--line)] underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:decoration-[var(--green)]"
              >GitHub</a
            >, including{" "}
            <a
              href="https://github.com/popgenomics/DILS"
              class="text-[var(--green)] underline decoration-[var(--line)] underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:decoration-[var(--green)]"
              >DILS</a
            >.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Contact -->
        <section id="contact" class="scroll-mt-8 py-12 lg:py-16">
          <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-12">
            <div>
              <h2 class="section-title">Contact</h2>
              <address class="mt-5 not-italic text-base leading-7">
                <p class="font-semibold text-[var(--foreground)]">Camille Roux</p>
                <p class="mt-1 text-[var(--muted)]">CNRS researcher</p>
                <p class="text-[var(--muted)]">
                  Institut des Sciences de l'Évolution de Montpellier
                </p>
                <p class="text-[var(--muted)]">Montpellier, France</p>
                <p class="mt-3">
                  <a
                    href="mailto:camille.roux@cnrs.fr"
                    class="text-[var(--green)] underline decoration-[var(--line)] underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:decoration-[var(--green)]"
                    >camille.roux@cnrs.fr</a
                  >
                </p>
              </address>
            </div>

            <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3 text-[0.95rem] lg:pt-6" role="list">
              <li>
                <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[var(--muted)]"
                  >Google Scholar</span
                >
                <a
                  href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=QppHnSsAAAAJ&hl=fr&oi=ao"
                  class="mt-1 block text-[var(--green)] underline decoration-[var(--line)] underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:decoration-[var(--green)]"
                  >scholar.google.com</a
                >
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[var(--muted)]"
                  >ISEM profile</span
                >
                <a
                  href="https://isem-evolution.fr/membre/roux/"
                  class="mt-1 block text-[var(--green)] underline decoration-[var(--line)] underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:decoration-[var(--green)]"
                  >isem-evolution.fr</a
                >
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[var(--muted)]"
                  >GitHub</span
                >
                <a
                  href="https://github.com/popgenomics/"
                  class="mt-1 block text-[var(--green)] underline decoration-[var(--line)] underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:decoration-[var(--green)]"
                  >github.com/popgenomics</a
                >
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
